# Performance And SEO

## Performance

- Prefer Server Components and server data fetching when interactivity is not needed.
- Use dynamic imports only for heavy or rarely used client components, not as a default.
- Avoid unnecessary client boundaries, effects, and global state.
- Keep repeated expensive computations in helpers, constants, memoized values, or server code based on where they run.
- Optimize lists by extracting stable item components when rendering becomes expensive or complex.
- Use `next/image` for raster images with explicit `width`/`height` (or `fill` + `sizes`). Add `priority` only for the above-the-fold LCP image.
- Use `next/font` for fonts; prefer variable fonts and do not list weights for them.

## Rendering

- Choose SSG, SSR, ISR, or client rendering intentionally. Default to static or ISR for public pages, and check the `npm run build` route table (○ static, ƒ dynamic) after changes.
- Set `cache`, `revalidate`, or `tags` explicitly when data freshness matters. Cache Components is disabled, so do not use `"use cache"` or `instant`.
- Avoid `cookies()`, `headers()`, and other dynamic APIs in pages that should stay static. Move per-user data into client components instead of making a whole route dynamic.
- Do not fetch the same data in multiple layers of the same route unless required; identical `serverFetch` calls are memoized per request (unless they pass a `signal`).

## SEO

- Use the Next.js Metadata API for indexable pages. `metadataBase` is set in the root layout from `BASE_URL`, so use relative URLs for images and canonicals.
- Set `alternates.canonical` per page (`ROUTES.x`), never in a layout — layout metadata is inherited and would point every child page at the same URL.
- Keep page titles, descriptions, headings, and Open Graph fields aligned with the actual page content. Page titles fill the root `"%s | Next.js Boilerplate"` template.
- Register new indexable routes in `src/app/sitemap.ts` (using `ROUTES`), and keep `src/app/robots.ts` and `src/app/manifest.ts` in sync when route structure or branding changes. Never list routes that do not exist.
- Mark non-indexable pages (404, auth, dashboards) with `robots: { index: false }`.
- Use one `h1` per page and semantic headings without skipping levels.
